From: Max 3 Pro device tree <max3pro@localhost>
Subject: [PATCH] max3pro: MIPI DSI panel and backlight

Drive the built-in 480x854 ST7701 panel of the ODROID-GO Ultra / RGB10
Max 3 Pro from U-Boot, with its PWM backlight. Mainline U-Boot has the
Synopsys DSI host, the AXG D-PHY and the Meson PWM, but not the Meson
DSI output, so this adds:

- meson_dw_mipi_dsi: the G12 DSI glue (port of the Linux driver). The
  U-Boot clock driver doesn't model GP0/VCLK2/ENCL/DSI pxclk, so it sets
  them in the HHI registers like the Hardkernel BSP U-Boot does: GP0 =
  lane bit rate (integer multiplier, pixel clock rounded to match), DSI
  bit clock = GP0, ENCL = GP0 / (bpp / lanes).
- ENCL setup in the VPU (port of meson_venc_mipi_dsi_mode_set). The VPU
  uses the DSI panel when the bridge is present, else HDMI/CVBS as before.
- phy-meson-g12a-mipi-dphy-analog (port of the Linux driver), AXG D-PHY
  allowed on G12A, MIPI DSI host/PHY clock gates.
- sitronix-st7701: the "odroid,go-ultra-panel" init sequence and mode from
  the Linux driver. The panel supply (vcc_lcd, RK817 LDO8) gets its fixed
  3.3 V set before it is enabled: U-Boot only applies constraints to
  boot-on regulators, so after a power-off the panel stayed dark at the
  LDO's reset voltage (a reboot kept the 3.3 V Linux had set).
- Device tree: panel, backlight (pwm_ef channel 1 = GPIOH_5, on the xtal
  with the old PWM binding U-Boot knows), DSI and D-PHY nodes enabled. The
  panel's rotation (270) turns the console (CONSOLE_ROTATION).
- pwm-meson: find the xtal ("fixed_clock" driver, the PWM driver looked
  for "fixed_rate_clock" and failed to probe, so no backlight), and two
  inverted register masks.
- CONSOLE_RECORD + "fastboot oem console": read the U-Boot log over USB
  (fastboot mode: VOLUME-UP + VOLUME-DOWN), the board has no serial port.

The framebuffer pipeline for the kernel is "vpu-dsi"; without such a
simplefb node in the kernel DT it is only reserved.

---
diff --git a/arch/arm/dts/meson-g12b-odroid-go-ultra-u-boot.dtsi b/arch/arm/dts/meson-g12b-odroid-go-ultra-u-boot.dtsi
index daffe065..b9c4016a 100644
--- a/arch/arm/dts/meson-g12b-odroid-go-ultra-u-boot.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm/dts/meson-g12b-odroid-go-ultra-u-boot.dtsi
@@ -73,3 +73,54 @@
 		remote-endpoint = <&hdmi_connector_in>;
 	};
 };
+
+/*
+ * Built-in 480x854 MIPI DSI panel (ST7701, same on the ODROID-GO Ultra and
+ * the RGB10 Max 3 Pro) and its PWM backlight, as in the kernel device tree.
+ * When enabled, the VPU uses the panel instead of HDMI.
+ */
+/ {
+	panel_backlight: backlight {
+		compatible = "pwm-backlight";
+		pwms = <&pwm_ef 1 40000 0>;
+		brightness-levels = <0 255>;
+		default-brightness-level = <255>;
+	};
+};
+
+/* U-Boot's PWM driver only knows the old binding: both channels on the xtal */
+&pwm_ef {
+	compatible = "amlogic,meson-g12a-ee-pwm";
+	clocks = <&xtal>, <&xtal>;
+	clock-names = "clkin0", "clkin1";
+	pinctrl-0 = <&pwm_f_h_pins>;
+	pinctrl-names = "default";
+	status = "okay";
+};
+
+&mipi_analog_dphy {
+	status = "okay";
+};
+
+&mipi_dphy {
+	status = "okay";
+};
+
+/* The DSI glue sets the GP0/VCLK2/ENCL clocks itself */
+&mipi_dsi {
+	status = "okay";
+	/delete-property/ assigned-clocks;
+	/delete-property/ assigned-clock-parents;
+	#address-cells = <1>;
+	#size-cells = <0>;
+
+	panel@0 {
+		compatible = "odroid,go-ultra-panel", "sitronix,st7701";
+		reg = <0>;
+		reset-gpios = <&gpio GPIOH_4 GPIO_ACTIVE_HIGH>;
+		IOVCC-supply = <&vcc_lcd>;
+		VCC-supply = <&vcc_lcd>;
+		backlight = <&panel_backlight>;
+		rotation = <270>;
+	};
+};
